.TH AS 1 "July 4, 2026" "ReBSD"
.SH NAME
as \- ReBSD MIPS assembler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B as
[
.B \-gkuvxX
]
[
.B \-o
.I outfile
]
[
.B \-I
.I dir
]
[
.B \-EL
|
.B \-EB
]
[
.B \-mips3
|
.B \-march=vr4300
|
.B \-mips32
]
[
.I infile
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B as
assembles MIPS source into the ReBSD
.B a.out
object format used by the native toolchain.
The accepted input syntax is the GCC/PCC MIPS assembler syntax emitted by
the ReBSD C compiler driver.
.PP
If
.I infile
is not specified, input is read from standard input.
The output file defaults to
.IR a.out ;
normal compiler invocations pass
.B \-o
explicitly.
.PP
The assembler supports the standard ReBSD text, data, bss, rodata,
constructor, destructor, and exception-frame sections, MIPS relocation
records, and the
.B .set reorder
and
.B .set noreorder
instruction scheduling modes required by compiler output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " outfile"
Write the object file to
.IR outfile .
.TP
.B \-u
Treat undefined symbols as errors.
.TP
.B \-x
Discard local symbols.
.TP
.B \-X
Discard local symbols whose names start with
.B L
or
.BR . .
.TP
.B \-EL
Emit little-endian
.B a.out
objects.
.TP
.B \-EB
Emit big-endian
.B a.out
objects.
.TP
.B \-mips3
.TQ
.B \-march=vr4300
Enable the VR4300-compatible instruction checks used by the N64 and
Malta64 compatibility ports.
Instructions known to require later MIPS32 revisions are rejected.
.TP
.B \-mips32
.TQ
.BI \-march= mips32
Use the generic MIPS32 acceptance mode.
.TP
.BI \-I " dir"
Accepted for compiler-driver compatibility.
.TP
.B \-g
.TQ
.B \-k
.TQ
.BI \-O level
Accepted for compiler-driver compatibility.
.TP
.B \-\-target-info
Print the assembler target defaults and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /tmp/asXXXXXX
Temporary files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cc (1),
.BR pcc (1),
.BR ld (1),
.BR nm (1),
.BR a.out (5)
